<title>USA: John Wiley Q1 net rises after buyout costs.</title>
<headline>John Wiley Q1 net rises after buyout costs.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>John Wiley &amp; Sons Inc.</p>
<p>				  Summary of Operations</p>
<p>						  First Quarter Ended</p>
<p>							July 31,</p>
<p>						     1996	     1995</p>
<p> Revenues				$ 99,217,000    $ 88,092,000</p>
<p> Operating income			11,716,000	11,496,000</p>
<p> Income before taxes		   11,295,000	11,864,000</p>
<p> Net income				 7,229,000	 7,118,000</p>
<p>Net income per share</p>
<p>  Primary &amp; fully diluted		    0.44		 .43</p>
<p>Average shares</p>
<p>  Primary				  16,518,000	16,448,000</p>
<p>  Fully diluted			  16,526,000	16,458,000</p>
<p>NOTE - Current quarter includes the results of VCH Publishing Group since date of acquisition in June 1996, which had the effect of increasing revenues by about six percent and reducing net income by $1.0 million, or $0.06 per share, primarily due to amortization of intangibles and financing costs related to the acquisition.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610</p>
</text>
